exports[`ExportReadiness over the sample projects > audits PaceGuard.agenticdesign 2`] = `
"NOT A WORKING APP — 1 blocker(s). The screens promise more than the binary can do.

[BLOCKER] Firebase flows exist, but Firebase is not configured
  No project credentials, so no GoogleService-Info.plist can be generated and FirebaseApp.configure() traps at launch. Call set_firebase_config with the Firebase console's projectId / apiKey / appId / messagingSenderId (Project settings ▸ your iOS app), then re-export — the plist is then written into the app target for you.

[INFO] 3 sensor block(s) will read real hardware
  Location uses CLLocation.distance with accuracy/jitter filtering; Health uses HealthKit. The Mac preview shows sample values — only a physical device proves them.

[INFO] Apple Watch: use export_xcode_project for a real watch app
  export_xcode_project produces a genuine watchOS App target (WatchWorkoutService — HKWorkoutSession + live heart rate — and PhoneWatchSync) embedded into the iPhone app; both targets build and the watch app runs on a watch. The SwiftPM export (export_ios_source) CANNOT build a watch bundle — there the watch screens only run inside the phone app. Pick the Xcode export to ship the watch."
`;

